{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01JcuNhBMazrWcs9wppndCoB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q37: Agents collaborating on research reports with citations**:\n\n**Architecture:** A 5-role supervisor/worker pipeline:\n1. **Planner** — decomposes the research question into a structured JSON outline with sub-queries per section\n2. **Researcher agents (parallel)** — each searches a distinct source domain (web, internal docs, arXiv) and returns structured `{claim, supporting_chunk, source_url, confidence}` JSON — *not* free-form prose\n3. **Orchestrator dedup step** — cosine-dedup retrieved chunks (> 0.92 threshold) before synthesis to prevent redundant citations\n4. **Synthesizer** — produces prose with inline `[n]` citation markers at T=0.3\n5. **Citation Validator** — independent NLI agent (DeBERTa-v3-large) verifies every citation entails its claim; flags score < 0.75 for revision or removal; max 2 revision loops\n\n**Key pitfalls covered:**\n- Researchers returning free-form prose instead of structured claim-evidence pairs → can't validate provenance\n- Trusting the Synthesizer to self-verify citations (conflating generation and entailment roles)\n- Not surfacing conflicting claims across Researchers → confident synthesis of contradictory evidence is the #1 hallucination mode\n- Skipping the orchestrator dedup step → duplicate-source bibliography entries\n\nTwo plan items remain: Q38 and the validate run."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":403,"cache_read_input_tokens":69077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":403,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7038b3a7-ff66-4fcd-a8d8-bd7acc349e61","uuid":"eebb4696-4d8d-4dbe-9195-aca203b75d56"}
